error[E0277]: `String` has no `.length` for a template to count
  --> tests/ui/length_of_a_string.rs:14:28
   |
14 |     let _ = template::page(String::from("Dub"));
   |             -------------- ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this value is not a list
   |             |
   |             required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `Length` is not implemented for `String`
   = note: `{{ x.length }}` counts a list — a `Vec`, a slice or an array. A `String` has no `.length` here: JS counts UTF-16 code units and Rust counts bytes or `char`s, so any answer would silently disagree with handlebars.js
   = help: the following other types implement trait `Length`:
             &T
             Absent<T>
             Vec<T>
             [T; N]
             [T]
             typed_handlebars::Empty
note: required by a bound in `page`
  --> tests/ui/length_of_a_string.rs:5:5
   |
 5 |     typed_handlebars::str!("page", r#"<h1>{{ title.length }}</h1>"#);
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `page`
   = note: this error originates in the macro `typed_handlebars::str` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

